(D2 — Discrepancy 2 repro: the `otherwise` clause the manual documents
 (LANGUAGE.md:2960, 2966) used to be a parse error after a `print` base
 action while being accepted after an `append` base.
 **RESOLVED — fixed by vox #50 (0.4.8+).** The bare spelling now compiles
 after `print` too, and this probe records the fixed behaviour: it
 compiles and takes the `otherwise` branch. Before #50 it failed to
 compile with `error: Expected a statement, got Otherwise`. The three
 neighbouring spellings compiled then and still do:
   print gauge, but if ... print "high", but otherwise print "low".   -> low
   append 1 to kept, but if ... append 7, otherwise append 9.         -> [9]
   append 1 to kept, but if ... append 7, but otherwise append 9.     -> [9]
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox D2.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   low
)
